# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X (-nocursor) +
# VICE xpet at the CBM 8032's own untouched power-on screen. Nothing is curated
# into the fixture and nothing is typed after the restore. (The Plus/4 add
# shipped a golden curated inside an application and had to be re-baked: it
# dropped visitors into the middle of a program with no way to tell what it was
# or how to leave. Bake the state the machine itself chose.)
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore CBM 8032 (1980) at its own untouched power-on screen: "*** commodore basic 4.0 *** / 31743 bytes free / ready." in green on black with a solid block cursor, 80 columns wide, drawn double-size (-CRTCdsize) by VICE xpet on a 1600x1200 X root — the tightest advertised mode that contains the 1408x1064 SDL window, and the 4:3 shape of the machine's own 12-inch monitor. No colour, no sprites and no sound generator: the 8032 had none. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device. The interaction is the registry demoProgram, a BASIC 4.0 times table that fills all 80 columns, typed by the SPA and started by the visitor's own RETURN.

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# Four frames each way, not the playbook's usual two. The 8032's 80-column
# editor ROM is the 50 Hz (European) one — edit-4-80-b-50Hz.901474-04_.bin, the
# ROM `-model 8032` selects — so a frame is 20 ms and two frames would be 40/40.
# Those numbers were BISECTED on the VIC-20, same emulator and same host
# (scripts/dev/emu-key-pacing-bisect.py: 40/40 corrupted 1 line in 22, 80/80
# none in 22), and are carried over rather than re-measured: the failure they
# guard against is a host scheduling stall on a box running 30+ emulators, which
# is a property of the box and not of the emulated machine. Re-bisect this tile
# if it ever drops characters.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
# Keep registry demoProgram.perCharMs >= 160 in step with these two: the SPA
# typist waits line.length * perCharMs before submitting the next line, and
# under-waiting builds a backlog whose symptom is missing characters.
# scripts/stations-registry.py validate_demo_pacing enforces it.
# No SH_KEY_MAP and no registry `keyboard` block. The 8032 has the BUSINESS
# keyboard (KBD_TYPE_BUSINESS_UK in VICE's petmodel.c), and VICE's matching
# symbolic keymap sdl_buuk_sym.vkm maps host ASCII straight onto that matrix —
# every character of the demo listing, including $ ( ) * ; : and -, was verified
# by framebuffer to arrive as itself. Unlike the VIC-20 this machine is NOT
# upper-case-only either: the business editor ROM comes up in text mode, where
# an unshifted letter displays as lower case and BASIC accepts it, which is why
# the registry listing is written in lower case and needs no letterCase flag.
